  "id": "orphenadrine",
  "term": "orphenadrine",
  "definition": "Orphenadrine is a drug with muscle-relaxing effects that acts as a muscarinic antagonist. It appears to block muscarinic acetylcholine and NMDA receptors in the central nervous system, which may reduce nerve signaling from the spinal cord to muscles; it also has blocking effects at histamine H1 receptors.",
